      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(cron): serve cron run history from the task ledger",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOne cron execution today produces three overlapping records: a rich `cron_run_logs` row, a deliberately thin `task_runs` mirror (silent, `not_applicable`, best-effort), and a session-registry row — plus dual-written `CronJobState` last-run fields. Downstream, task maintenance needs a cron-specific recovery branch that cross-reads two cron stores, and the Control UI shows the same execution twice at different fidelity (Automations run history vs Tasks page).\n\nPart 1 of 2 for #106041: make the task ledger the authoritative record for cron executions and flip the external read paths, while keeping the legacy `cron_run_logs` dual-write as a revert safety net. PR 2 migrates old history, deletes the run-log stack, and unifies cancellation.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- `task_runs` gains a generic nullable `detail_json` column (additive `ensureColumn` migration + regenerated Kysely types). Cron owns the codec ([task-run-detail.ts](../blob/HEAD/src/cron/task-run-detail.ts)) between run outcomes, ledger detail, and the **unchanged** `CronRunLogEntry` wire shape.\n- Cron writes full-fidelity terminal rows (status vocabulary, delivery trace, `errorReason`, `triggerFired`, `nextRunAtMs`, model/usage) instead of the lobotomized mirror; skipped runs now create immediately-terminal rows so history parity holds.\n- `cron.runs` RPC, the CLI run-history poll, and task-maintenance cron recovery read from the ledger ([task-run-history.ts](../blob/HEAD/src/cron/task-run-history.ts)); the maintenance cron branch shrinks from two cross-store readers to a ledger self-lookup, and `configureTaskRegistryMaintenance` loses its `cronStorePath` parameter.\n- Startup crash recovery improves: a run that finished before the crash is restored from its finalized ledger row (with `record-only` failure-alert cooldown restore) instead of being reported as \"interrupted\".\n- Same-millisecond executions get distinct ledger rows via a run-id discriminator; the reservation timestamp keys recovery.\n\n- Existing history migrates automatically: a one-shot state migration ([state-migrations.cron-run-logs.ts](../blob/HEAD/src/infra/state-migrations.cron-run-logs.ts)) imports `cron_run_logs` rows into the ledger at first DB open — no manual doctor step — with deterministic import ids for idempotency and dual-write-aware duplicate matching.\n- History reads stay scoped to the configured cron store: `cron_run_logs` partitions by `store_key`, so ledger detail records the store key and `readCronTaskRunHistoryPage` filters by it (kept out of the wire shape; test-locked).\n\nNon-goals here (PR 2): stopping the dual-write, dropping `cron_run_logs` + `cron.runLog.*` config keys, per-source retention, cancel unification. No protocol schema, UI, or config changes; `CronRunLogEntrySchema` consumers (Control UI, macOS, Android) see identical responses.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo visible behavior change. Cron run history is served from the shared task ledger; Automations history and the Tasks page now describe the same rows. Crash-interrupted-but-completed runs report their true outcome after restart instead of a synthetic interruption error.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Parity tests: ledger-served history equals legacy run-log responses across ok/error/timeout/skipped, delivery statuses, trigger, telemetry, paging, and text-query filtering (`src/cron/task-run-history.test.ts`).\n- Race matrix: operator-cancel precedence, lost-row overwrite, same-ms collisions, skip rows (`src/cron/service/task-runs.test.ts`, `ops.test.ts`, `timer.test.ts`).\n- Serialized-detail shape locked behind the indexed LIKE prefixes so codec field reordering fails loudly.\n- **Production-data migration proof**: against a copied 247 MB production state DB (2,750 legacy run-log rows, 5 jobs, 952 pre-upgrade task rows): 2,750/2,750 imported, 0 malformed, ledger vs legacy reader totals equal and first page byte-identical, second open idempotent (no double import).\n- Focused packs green locally (~1,750 tests across cron/tasks/gateway/infra surfaces); structured second-model review run to zero accepted findings (two accepted findings fixed: legacy runId recovery, store-key scoping + auto-migration); full gates on hosted CI/Testbox.\n",
